:: work {"position":"700,250"}
<<scenery dump>>
<<set if(!$player.job.hours)$player.job.hours=8>>\
<<addHours $player.job.hours>>\
<<set $player.workedToday = true>>\
You spend $player.job.hours hours working on your job as $player.job.name
<<cash $player.job.pay>>
You currently own ¤<<- $player.cash.toFixed(2)>>

<<keyOption [[Return home|home]] 🏠>>

<<if $slaves.length gt 1 >>
    <<set
        _hungryBasementSlaveCount = Basement.getHungrySlaves().length;
        _neededPizzas = Math.ceil((_hungryBasementSlaveCount * 3) / 8);
        _pizzasPrice = _neededPizzas * 9;
    >>\
    <<if _hungryBasementSlaveCount && !Player.has("pizza", _neededPizzas) && $player.cash gte _pizzasPrice>>\
        <<keyAction "Go buy pizza for all the hungry slaves in the basement (¤_pizzasPrice) and return home" 🍕>>\
            <<run
                $player.cash -= _pizzasPrice;
                Player.getInventory().add({
                    name:'Pizza',
                    description:'Median basic pizza',
                    count:_neededPizzas,
                    tags: ["player", "food", "consumable"]
                })
            >>
            <<addMinutes 10>>
            <<goto home>>
        <</keyAction>>: 10min detour\
    <</if>>\
<</if>>\
:: home {"position":"700,375"}
<<scenery home>>
You are currently in front of your home.
<<unlessEmergency>>
    <<keyOption [[Go inside|main]] 🚪>>
    <<include workOption>>\
    <<keyOption [[Go to the park|playground]] ⚽>>
    <<keyOption [[Go to the school|shool]] 🏫>>
    <<keyOption [[Go to alleys|alleys]] 🏙️>>
<</unlessEmergency>>\




:: centralPlaza
<<scenery Plaza>>

You head down the road a little ways, and think you can see the Towns Plaza dead ahead. <<addMinutes 7>> 
It takes you about 7 minutes to reach the Plaza and once you arrive you are rather surprised to see that the Plaza
isn't bustling as much as you thought it would be... Everyone must be in the other parts of town. You
look around for a map of some sort. But the closest thing you can find is a Signpost that says
Welcome to Honeycross, please enjoy your stay! It is clearly meant for tourists not the locals.
Underneath the welcome sign there are four arrows one pointing towards each District Of Honeycross.


Where would you like to go?

